      "role": "user",
      "content": "Can you summarize the specific steps our company needs to follow when we receive a formal \"Right to be Forgotten\" request from a user, according to GDPR guidelines? We need to make sure we aren't missing any technical or administrative requirements for complete data erasure.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To comply with GDPR guidelines when receiving a \"Right to be Forgotten\" request, follow these steps:\n\n1. Acknowledge the request promptly.\n2. Verify the identity of the individual.\n3. Remove personal data from your records.\n4. Ensure all copies are deleted across all databases and storage systems, including backups.\n5. Inform any third parties with whom you share the data of the erasure.\n6. Keep documentation of the requests and responses for future references. \n7. Conduct a thorough review to ensure no traces of the data remain. \n\nRemember to revisit your data management processes to prevent future occurrences and stay updated with the latest regulatory changes.",
      "source": "target",
